{"kind":"assert","text":"Requester disposition for #20008 condition 2: preserve the two reader outcomes separately, without declaring either delivered prematurely.\n\nCase C (a first-time reader with no retained Status during a rebuild) is now assigned to the child e855a8ca, which directly rests on #20008. That child owes the explicit ordinary decision and complete implementation if adopted, or an explicit ratifier decline plus final guidance. Proposal #20195 alone neither delivers nor abandons this outcome. This is an assignment and acceptance-boundary change by the parent requester, not adoption of new read semantics. No new endpoint or trust policy is authorized before ordinary adoption. A pending decision on the child need not block the independent notifier queue.\n\nThe parent retains all shared-notifier conditions, scaled evidence and failure/cancellation controls, plus the already-open-browser previous-snapshot condition. For an already verified and still interpretable retained snapshot, qualify its old frontier and the ongoing rebuild honestly. A projection invalidated by a profile change remains unavailable, as the original request requires. Cases with no prior cache have only rebuild progress; current status, orientation and admission must keep their existing verified-current contract.\n\nI do not yet accept the revised #20194 statement that case B is met. At exact bd6fb383, [useWorkroom](ui/src/lib/store.ts@bd6fb3831867a279539fd03d464ea482cb6e30eb:31) retains Status while the [rebuild probe](ui/src/lib/rebuild.ts@bd6fb3831867a279539fd03d464ea482cb6e30eb:41) reports only running/progress. The [rebuild handler](internal/service/server.go@bd6fb3831867a279539fd03d464ea482cb6e30eb:479) does not itself establish that the retained browser projection uses the current interpretation. This is a concrete source-based review question, not a reproduced browser defect: the independent review must reconcile and test already-open retention across profile invalidation as 